# Frame and overlays: a watermark is a Page overlay with Layer: -1 behind the content of every page, with a faint image.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Frame and overlays · Watermark
	Page:
		Paper: A5
		Margin: 40
	Page overlay:
		Layer: -1
		Offset: 0
		Box:
			Width: 260
			Height: 260
			Margin: auto
		Image: examples/menu/emblem.svg
			Opacity: 12%
			Box:
				Width: 100%
	Section:
		Text: Frame and overlays
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Watermark
		Paragraph: The emblem is a `Page overlay` with `Layer: -1`, painted beneath the content on every page. With `Offset: 0`, a size and `Margin: auto` it is centered in the page area, and the image inside is made faint with `Opacity: 12%`.
			Style: intro
		Paragraph: The text of the page is painted over the watermark. The contrast of a text over an image is not checked, so the image is kept faint.
		Paragraph: The second page carries the same watermark.
			Break:
				Before: page
